Mini Project DiceMan

Assignment: The Dice Man’s Daily Destiny
Every morning, The Dice Man wakes up and doesn’t know what to do. Instead of deciding like a normal person, he casts a dice ●  . The dice chooses his entire day:
1.	Eat breakfast
2.	Study something boring
3.	Go swimming
4.	Go fishing  • •
5.	Call his mom
6.	Go back to bed
The problem? The Dice Man doesn’t stop after one roll. He keeps rolling until he has done 5 activities for the day. Your mission: program the life of the Dice Man in Java.


Advanced Challenge
Count how many times he “went back to bed.” If it happens 3 times or more, end the day early with:
"The Dice Man got too lazy and stayed in bed forever..."


Tip: How to generate random numbers in Java
In Java you usually have two easy options:
1.	Using Random class (recommended in OOP): Random rand = new Random();
int dice = rand.nextInt(6) + 1; // 1–6
2.	Using Math.random() (quick & simple):
int dice = (int)(Math.random() * 6) + 1; // 1–6

 Math.random() always gives a number between 0.0 and 1.0. Multiplying by 6 makes it 0–5.something, and (int) cuts it down to an integer. Adding +1 makes it 1–6.

